---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="about — colin vargas"
  description="I’m Colin Vargas, an aerospace engineering graduate from ASU. I’m interested in what happens when you put more of the physics into a flow or combustion model."
>
  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
    <section class="page-intro" aria-labelledby="about-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span>Houston → Arizona</span>
      </div><h1 id="about-title">
        hey, i’m colin<span class="accent-dot">.</span>
      </h1><div class="intro-bottom">
        <p>
          i grew up in Houston and came to Arizona to study aerospace at ASU.
          i minored in French and took graduate courses in 2025–2026.
          airplanes got me into engineering, and now i’m especially interested
          in what happens when you put more of the physics into a flow model.
        </p><p class="intro-note">
          right now i’m working on scalar advection in AMReX. i want to get
          the single-grid case right before i add adaptive refinement.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="about-story" aria-labelledby="thinking-title">
      <span class="eyebrow">what got me into modeling</span><div>
        <h2 id="thinking-title">what did the model leave out?</h2><p>
          i like tracking a result back to the choice that produced it. was
          it the physics, a boundary condition, or just how i discretized an
          equation? a small case makes that a lot easier to figure out.
        </p><p>
          at Honeywell i helped sort through case notes and emulator output
          for aircraft already in service. with the ASU Solar Devils, i got to
          see what happens when an aeroshell design has to fit the car, meet
          the rules, and be ready in time to build.
        </p><a class="text-link" href="/work"
          >see my projects <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        >
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="portfolio-section" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2 id="principles-title">a few things i’ve learned</h2>
      </div><ol class="project-approach">
        <li>
          <h3>
            check one thing at a time
          </h3><p>
            a problem with a known solution gives me somewhere to look when
            the code does something weird.
          </p>
        </li><li>
          <h3>
            pay attention to the odd result
          </h3><p>
            in the winglet lab, some of the drag values made me go back to
            how the forces were measured and reduced.
          </p>
        </li><li>
          <h3>
            save the setup with the plot
          </h3><p>
            i want to be able to rerun the case without guessing which values
            i used the first time.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>
    <section class="beyond-grid about-beyond">
      <h2>outside of school</h2><div>
        <p>
          i’m learning to fly. i also run a homelab, which started with making
          things work and turned into wondering how i’d know when they stopped.
        </p><a class="text-link" href="/systems"
          >my homelab status page <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        >
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="page-next">
      <span class="eyebrow">research and projects</span><a href="/contact"
        >get in touch <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
      >
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
